{{!-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     One written page of the Notes tab.

     This exists because the decision it makes was written out eight times, and
     every one of the eight had the same bug:

         {{#if details.bio}}   <div>…the html…</div>
         {{else if unlocked}}  <textarea …></textarea>

     Read that again. The editor appears only when the field is EMPTY. A page
     could be written once and never edited afterwards — and the textarea was
     rendered with nothing between its tags anyway, so even that first write
     started from blank no matter what was already stored.

     One place now, and the rule is the other way round: unlocked, there is an
     editor, and it holds what is there; locked, the text is shown as a5e
     enriched it.

     Takes:  label   the heading
             text    the field as plain text, for the editor
             html    the field as stored, for reading
             path    where to write it, e.g. system.details.bio
             hint    placeholder for an empty one
             flat    true to leave the heading off (the four personality
                     fields sit under one shared heading)
     ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
{{#if @root.unlocked}}
  <textarea class="am-bio-input" data-action="detail-html"
    data-path="{{path}}" aria-label="{{label}}"
    placeholder="{{hint}}">{{text}}</textarea>
{{else if html}}
  <div class="am-origin-desc">{{{html}}}</div>
{{/if}}
